drivers: i2c: mspm0: fix controller receive deadlock and multi-interrupt handling

1. Fix controller receive deadlock on short reads (<= 8 bytes):
   When receiving small packets that fit within the 8-byte MSPM0 RX FIFO,
   the STOP condition occurs while data->state is still I2C_MSPM0_RX_STARTED.
   Previously, the STOP handler only acted if state == I2C_MSPM0_RX_INPROGRESS,
   silently dropping the STOP event and leaving device_sync_sem un-signaled,
   which deadlocked k_sem_take(..., K_FOREVER).
   Fix this by draining any remaining RX FIFO bytes and signaling device_sync_sem
   for both RX_STARTED and RX_INPROGRESS states.

2. Loop over all pending interrupts in i2c_mspm0_isr_controller:
   DL_I2C_getPendingInterrupt() returns the highest priority interrupt and
   clears it. When multiple interrupt events fire simultaneously (e.g.
   RXFIFO_TRIGGER followed immediately by STOP), evaluate all pending interrupts
   in a loop until DL_I2C_IIDX_NO_INT.

3. Unconditionally signal device_sync_sem on NACK and ARBITRATION_LOST:
   Ensure error states immediately release waiting threads instead of hanging.

4. Add 100ms safety timeouts to k_sem_take(device_sync_sem) in receive/transmit:
   Prevent indefinite kernel lockups if bus glitches or hardware lockups occur.

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/i2c_mspm0.c b/drivers/i2c/i2c_mspm0.c
